<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hassan ibn Thabit</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 674</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hassan ibn Thabit was an Arab poet of the Khazraj tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>. Before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> he praised the Ghassanid kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, and after his conversion he became the leading poet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>, defending him and the Muslims in verse against their opponents. His collected poems are an important source for early Islamic history.</p></div>
